@startuml how_a_starved_state_reaches_the_value
title How a starved state reaches the value a node states

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Operator" as operator
participant "Feed graph" as graph
participant "Simulator fleet" as fleet
participant "Halted set" as halted
participant "Offers" as offers
participant "Feed" as feed
participant "Market data service" as marketdata

operator -> graph : stop a node
graph -> graph : rebuild the graph
graph -> halted : write the names that are not running
note right of halted
  A stopped node and every node
  below it, named once and held
  until the next rebuild.
end note

graph -> offers : withhold the offers of the halted names
offers -> marketdata : withdraw the demand
marketdata --> feed : the demand that started it is gone
note right of feed
  The offer path needs no other
  guard: a node nobody demands
  publishes nothing.
end note

halted -> feed : the set, on every tick
feed -> feed : read its own name in the set
alt the name is in the set
  feed --> marketdata : no tick
  note right of marketdata
    The value the input last wrote
    stays on the board, and the
    node states nothing for the day.
  end note
else the name is not in the set
  feed --> marketdata : the day's value
end

operator -> graph : start the node again
graph -> halted : rebuild, and the name leaves the set
graph -> offers : offer the node again
feed -> marketdata : the day it lands on, and no earlier one
note right of marketdata
  The days it was starved for stay
  absent: a fixing is a fact about
  a date, not a value to make up.
end note

@enduml
